    <statement><p>The function <m>f</m> has  a continuous
second derivative, and it satisfies <m>f(3) = -7</m>, <m>f'(3) = 0</m> and <m>f''(3) = 2</m>.</p>
<p>We can conclude that
<var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>f</m> has a local minimum at 3</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>f</m> has neither a local maximum nor a local minimum at 3</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>f</m> has a local maximum at 3</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>We cannot determine if A, B, or C hold without more information.</p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
